From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] keyhandler: repeat the first verdict for a duplicate dispatch

KeyHandler._key_pressed_cb is connected to several widgets - the shell
window, Home, the Journal and the Casilda compositor - so one physical press
reaches it once per widget on the propagation path. The duplicate guard
returned True for every repeat, which tells GTK the key was handled and
stops propagation, even for keys Sugar never acted on. A letter typed while
an Activity was focused was therefore consumed by the shell before the
compositor's own key controller could forward it to the Wayland client.

Remember whether the first dispatch actually handled the key and repeat that
verdict, so unhandled keys keep travelling to the focused Activity surface.

The guard this patch originally assumed - `self._last_dispatch` and the
`token == self._last_dispatch` block - existed only in the hand-edited
preview checkout and was never carried by any patch in the series, so the
patch could not apply to a clean baseline. It now introduces the whole
mechanism.

--- a/src/jarabe/view/keyhandler.py
+++ b/src/jarabe/view/keyhandler.py
@@ -82,6 +82,8 @@
         self._key_pressed = None
         self._keycode_pressed = 0
         self._keystate_pressed = 0
+        self._last_dispatch = None
+        self._last_dispatch_handled = False
         self._handled_windows = set()
 
         self._tabbing_handler = TabbingHandler(self._frame, _TABBING_MODIFIER)
@@ -239,6 +241,21 @@
             logging.warning("uitree module not available.")
 
     def _key_pressed_cb(self, controller, keyval, keycode, state):
+        event = controller.get_current_event()
+        if event is not None:
+            token = (keyval, keycode, int(state), event.get_time())
+            if token == self._last_dispatch:
+                # This handler is attached to several widgets, so one press
+                # arrives once per widget on the propagation path. Repeat the
+                # first verdict: claiming a key Sugar never acted on stops it
+                # before the focused Activity surface can receive it.
+                return self._last_dispatch_handled
+            self._last_dispatch = token
+        self._last_dispatch_handled = self._dispatch_key(
+            controller, keyval, keycode, state)
+        return self._last_dispatch_handled
+
+    def _dispatch_key(self, controller, keyval, keycode, state):
         key = Gdk.keyval_name(keyval)
         logging.warning("GTK4 semantic key event: %s", key)
         if not key:
